---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import { exhibits } from "../data/exhibits";
import "../styles/bookends.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — MATH × ART" description="About the MATH × ART digital exhibition.">
  <div class="about-shell">
    <SiteHeader current="about" />
    <main id="main-content" class="about-page">
      <header class="about-page__hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">About the exhibition</p>
        <h1>Mathematics is not only calculated. It can be seen, drawn, heard, and built.</h1>
      </header>

      <section class="about-page__grid" aria-label="Exhibition context">
        <div>
          <h2>The idea</h2>
          <p>
            MATH × ART is a small digital exhibition for MATH 10 work. Instead of
            imitating a three-dimensional museum, the site behaves like a quiet sequence
            of gallery walls: one work receives attention at a time, with a concise label
            and deliberate navigation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>The collection</h2>
          <p>
            The current collection contains {exhibits.length} works spanning mathematical
            graphing, geometric illustration, perspective drawing, and an interactive
            audiovisual sonification.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>The labels</h2>
          <p>
            Titles and descriptive text are intentionally conservative. Where an artist
            name has not yet been confirmed, the museum says so rather than guessing.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>The interactive work</h2>
          <p>
            Fibonacci, Modulo 25 remains a separate live artwork. The museum presents a
            preview and then hands control to the interactive piece, where sound starts
            only after the visitor chooses to play it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="about-page__cta">
        <a class="button button--dark" href="/exhibition">Explore the collection <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
